# Blocks piping jest through tail/head/grep.
#
# NOT once-per-session, unlike every other rule here: this is a hard stop on a
# mechanical mistake, not a nudge toward a skill. Making it spendable by doing it
# twice would defeat it.
#
# Why: jest writes massive output and tail/head/grep buffer ALL of it until the
# process exits, so the run looks hung for minutes. Rule lives in tests/README.md.
rule_id=jest-pipe
rule_once=0

rule_match() {
    [ "$1" = "Bash" ] || return 1
    printf '%s' "$2" | grep -qE '(^|[[:space:]/])jest[[:space:]][^|;]*\|[[:space:]]*(tail|head|grep)([[:space:]]|$)'
}

rule_message() {
    cat <<'MSG'
Blocked: never pipe jest through tail/head/grep — output buffering makes the run look hung.
Instead redirect to a file and read it:
  npx jest --no-coverage <pattern> > "$SCRATCH/jest-output.txt" 2>&1

Order matters: `> file 2>&1`, never `2>&1 > file` (that leaves the file empty).
Use your session scratchpad rather than /tmp.
MSG
}
